Package: fabricQueryR
Title: Query Data in 'Microsoft Fabric'
Version: 0.2.1.9000
Authors@R: 
    c(person(given = "Luka",
             family = "Koning",
             role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
             email = "koningluka@gmail.com"),
      person(given = "Kennispunt Twente",
             role = "fnd",
             email = "info@kennispunttwente.nl"))
Description: 
    Discover workspaces, items, and workload endpoints in 'Microsoft Fabric'.
    Provides helpers to open parameterized 'DBI' connections to 'SQL' endpoints
    of 'Lakehouse', 'Data Warehouse', and 'SQL Database' items; submit
    'Data Analysis Expressions' ('DAX') queries to semantic model datasets in 'Microsoft
    Fabric' and 'Power BI'; list, inspect, download, upload, and delete files
    in 'OneLake' ('Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2'), including direct 'R' and
    'Arrow' interchange with columnar files; discover and read 'Delta Lake'
    tables in 'OneLake'; stage data frames or existing CSV and Parquet files
    into managed Lakehouse tables; start, monitor, diagnose, and cancel semantic
    model refreshes; invoke published Fabric User Data Functions; execute
    'Kusto Query Language' ('KQL')
    queries against 'Eventhouse' databases; submit and monitor tracked queued
    ingestion from blob or 'OneLake' storage into existing 'Eventhouse' tables,
    including bounded staging of data frames and lazy 'Arrow' data;
    call user-configured 'GraphQL'
    APIs over Fabric data; and execute 'Spark' code via the 'Livy API'.
    Item jobs can be submitted, monitored, waited on, and cancelled, and their
    run history and recurring schedules can be managed through the Fabric Job
    Scheduler APIs. Fabric Core long-running operations can be resumed,
    monitored, and retrieved through a shared result contract.
